From: Jon Cory <jcory@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 22:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] visp_video: expose vb2 min_queued_buffers as a module
 parameter for single-buffer capture

The visp-video vb2 capture queue hardcodes min_queued_buffers = 5, which
forces REQBUFS(1) up to a 6-deep ring.  On the ERICA sentry ISP bridge the
single-buffer path needs the ISP to write ONE carveout window so the erica
RD-DMA (pinned at W0) reads the freshly written frame; the forced ring makes
the ISP round-robin across windows the RD-DMA never reads -> green/stale tiles.

Expose min_queued_buffers as a module parameter (default 0 = true single
buffer) so the ring depth is tunable at runtime without a rebuild.

Signed-off-by: Jon Cory <jcory@amd.com>
---
diff --git a/visp_video/visp_video_register.c b/visp_video/visp_video_register.c
index c584d28..c7e90b4 100644
--- a/visp_video/visp_video_register.c
+++ b/visp_video/visp_video_register.c
@@ -2893,6 +2893,17 @@ static const struct vb2_ops visp_video_queue_ops = {
 	.stop_streaming = visp_video_vb2_stop_streaming,
 };
 
+/* SINGLE-BUFFER support (ERICA sentry ISP-bridge).  vb2's default
+ * min_queued_buffers=5 forces REQBUFS(1) up to a 6-deep ring, so the ISP
+ * round-robins NV12 across windows the erica RD-DMA (pinned at W0) never
+ * reads -> green/stale tiles in single-buffer mode.  Expose it as a module
+ * parameter so the ring can be shrunk to a TRUE single buffer (0) at runtime
+ * without a rebuild.  Default 0 = single buffer. */
+static int visp_video_min_queued_buffers;
+module_param(visp_video_min_queued_buffers, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(visp_video_min_queued_buffers,
+        "vb2 min_queued_buffers (0 = true single buffer; default 0)");
+
 static int visp_video_queue_init(struct visp_video_dev *visp_vdev)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
@@ -2909,7 +2920,7 @@ static int visp_video_queue_init(struct visp_video_dev *visp_vdev)
 	queue->lock = &visp_vdev->video_lock;
 	queue->dev = visp_vdev->visp_mdev->dev;
 
-	queue->min_queued_buffers = 5;
+	queue->min_queued_buffers = visp_video_min_queued_buffers;
 
 	ret = vb2_queue_init(queue);
 	if (ret) {
-- 
